{"role":"assistant","content":"The bug is clear: `build_system()` (bot.py:130) concatenates the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the per-athlete context (which includes the growing `facts` list) into a single block with one cache marker. When `save_fact` appends a fact, the whole block changes, so the cache entry for the entire prefix is invalidated and ~1000 tokens of static rules get re-created — exactly the `cache_creation_input_tokens: ~1000, cache_read_input_tokens: 0` pattern in the log after every `save_fact`.\n\nLet me check the baseline git state and measure how big the static instructions are (relevant to cache-breakpoint limits).","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_lTgfliHZhP2UJXsYfZQpgs4T","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"git status --short && git log --oneline -3\",\"cwd\":\"/private/tmp/h-rHw09N\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_VkrtCBkAOEdmF2AFWeKHRcpm","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport bot, datetime\\na = bot.load_athlete(\\\"42\\\")\\nctx = bot.athlete_context(a, datetime.date.today())\\nprint(\\\"INSTRUCTIONS chars:\\\", len(bot.INSTRUCTIONS), \\\"approx tokens:\\\", len(bot.INSTRUCTIONS)//4)\\nprint(\\\"context chars:\\\", len(ctx), \\\"approx tokens:\\\", len(ctx)//4)\\nblocks = bot.build_system(a, datetime.date.today())\\nprint(\\\"blocks:\\\", len(blocks))\\nfor b in blocks:\\n    print(b.get(\\\"cache_control\\\"), repr(b[\\\"text\\\"][:60]))\\nEOF\",\"cwd\":\"/private/tmp/h-rHw09N\"}"}}]}
