{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The problem and the change:\n\n**Root cause** — `build_system()` (bot.py:130) built the system prompt as one block: static `INSTRUCTIONS` + athlete context (including the growing `facts` list), with a single `cache_control` marker. Anthropic hashes the whole prefix up to a breakpoint, so one appended fact changed the hash and invalidated the entire ~1000-token cached prefix — exactly the `cache_creation_input_tokens ~1000, cache_read_input_tokens: 0` rows in `logs/usage.jsonl` after every `save_fact`, even though a fact is only ~15 tokens.\n\n**Fix** — split the system prompt into two marked blocks, static first: the coaching rules as their own cache segment, then the per-athlete context as a second, small segment. A `save_fact` now only re-creates the ~100-token context block; the instructions stay cached and are read at cache price. The context block is also marked so unchanged context still hits within the 5-minute TTL. Uses 2 of the 4 allowed breakpoints; nothing else (tool selection, loop, logging) was touched.\n\n**Verified without API calls** — two-block shape and marker placement; the static block is byte-identical before/after a simulated `save_fact` while the context block reflects it; profile edits still flow through; `reply()` runs end-to-end with a stub LLM. The stub's log line and `__pycache__` were removed afterward — `logs/usage.jsonl` and `data/athletes.json` are untouched.\n\nFiles changed: `bot.py` (the split in `build_system()`) and `ANSWER.md` (full writeup, including two caveats: Sonnet 4.5's 1024-token minimum per breakpoint — a shorter segment silently isn't cached — and that tool-group keyword changes also bust the cache since tools precede the system prompt in the prefix, which I left alone per NOTES.md)."}
